# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-1 windows (the ship-5 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt, ORDER-W2.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the three runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-next-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory and, since NP9, with the output
# ceiling of its catalog entry; the keys are the same in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The prefix, replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader
# refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint, which is what their question (exactness of reuse against a cold twin of the same boot; the platform sequence) does not depend on.
# B0 (STOP): the WINDOW image tp4-next-1, built from the pushed tp4/next-1 head (the shipped ship-4 stack and its checkpoint selection plus NP1, NP9, exact resume P0, the
# sliced restore and the W3 WC lever, all default off): the APPROVED ship-4 profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4 baked as the serving default
# with a session cap of 8, plus C2_BAKE_GRAFT=K64j-OQ. The candidate c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5 is a profile of the file and is chosen by a
# job's C2_PROFILE; it cannot be the baked default while its owner traffic waiver is PENDING (ORDER-SHIP.txt, B1). READ: "baking the serving default
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4 with a session cap of 8", the provenance report with no problem line, its K64j-OQ graft line, the image id. A
# build, not a card job: it may run while production serves; no privileged builder container may be up and no card job may run during it. Estimate from the last builds:
# 35-40 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4
C2_BAKE_GRAFT=K64j-OQ
